data_two_chains
#
# Two chains, each long enough to spline (3 C-alphas), positioned so that a
# ribbon which ignores the chain break produces a leg that looks completely
# ordinary: chain A's C-terminus (6.800, 0, 0) and chain B's N-terminus
# (10.600, 0, 0) are 3.800 A apart -- the same C-alpha--C-alpha spacing used
# everywhere else in this file -- and collinear with chain A's final segment,
# so the spurious tube would be a smooth, plausible continuation of the
# backbone. Nothing about its length, direction or curvature gives it away;
# only the fact that geometry exists in the gap at all does.
#
# The two chains also sit in clearly separated pLDDT bands so per-chain color
# alignment is testable by position alone: chain A is 93-97 (the ">90" blue
# band) and chain B is 35-45 (the "<50" orange band). No interpolation within
# either chain can cross a ramp threshold, so every vertex of a correctly
# colored ribbon is unambiguously one band or the other.
#
loop_
